the US Military Academy at West Point is  investigating a deadly crash during a  training exercise the rollover yesterday  killed one cadet and left 21 others  injured Don Dahler is in Highland Falls  New York near the Academy so Don what do  we know about this accident good morning  to you good morning well the cadets were  here on a summer training program the  accident unfolded on the very same day  that the country pause to commemorate  the d-day celebrations or our  honorariums I should say the 75th  anniversary thereof and the  superintendent here at West Point  described this as a tragic day for the  community we don't know the details of  how the accident actually investigators  want to know exactly how a tactical  vehicle packed with cadets overturned in  the woods near the Academy early  Thursday morning they were headed to  land navigation training when they were  in the back of the the truck the light  medium tactical vehicle like the one  seen here had a soft canvas top and  weighed more than 11,000 pounds 20  cadets all rising seniors in the class  of 2020 were seated in the cargo bed of  the truck driven by two soldiers they  were said to be driving in rough terrain  you can see by looking around very hilly  we want to make sure that our soldiers  and our cadets train in realistic  training environment so this is a part  of our realistic training one cadet was  killed the 19 other cadets as well as  the two soldiers suffered  non-life-threatening injuries the West  Point superintendent said accidents like  these are rare but is not common for  these vehicles to turn over but it has  happened before  back in June 2016 at Fort Hood nine  soldiers died after their vehicle  flipped in a flood stream in 2009 13  were injured after their truck  overturned at Fort Bragg the  superintendent said the West Point  community is mourning but would respond  with strength I mean this is the United  States Army were strong we're strong  here at West Point president Trump  expressed his condolences via Twitter  calling this a terrible accident West  Point is expected to release the name of  the cadet later today gale Don thank you  very much
 

